From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanori-rider <rtanori1@asu.edu>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:51:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FFT: zero the fitter's path-B centering offset for battle
 rects

widefix10 left rect A and FIT_A full-width but FIT_B at (144,0,1776,888): the fitter's path-B offset (w2-w1)/2 = (1920-1632)/2 still centers the battle layer. Follow the fitter's own width chain (0x431c0 with w1=0, 0x41220, 0x3f954) to the u16 at [p3+0x48] for both objects and set them to 1920; widen rect B at [x6] only after both writes succeed, so a failed width write cannot push its right edge to 2064. Read the real x2 object from [r[8]] because the gate runs before the original ldr x2,[x8]. Keep the >=1500 width gate so UI rects are untouched (the earlier blanket gate caused darkness). Also raise the second object's aspect constant to 2.162 and extend DEBUG with both width fields and write results.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: FFT 1.5.1 battle picture was still confined to a centered 1632-wide rect (144 px bars) after rect A was widened. Zero the fitter's path-B centering offset by setting both objects' u16 width fields to 1920 and widening rect B only after both writes succeed; tighten the gate to battle-width rects so UI overlays keep their dims (no darkness). Fork product goal: edge-to-edge on a 19.5:9 iPhone panel.
Issue: mexicanstratocaster/NX2Apple-edgy#1

---
 dm/games/010038B015560000/patches.py |  5 +-
 dm/host/dm.h                         |  2 +-
 dm/host/hle_pillarbox.c              | 85 +++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 81 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

